! VFL STORE ROUNDED (SRD, VFL code 101101), hand-derived, eleven cases with
! the indicator register read after each.  Built 2026-11-16 (the ST arm of
! bsv/StretchExecute.bsv, which SRD shares; its header has the readings).
!
! SOURCE: Reference Manual 22-6530-2 printed p.64 (PDF 67), read in the
! page image:
!   "The field from the accumulator is rounded by adding to its magnitude
!   one-half of the proper radix in the position to the right of the
!   offset.  Carries are propagated as in any addition in that radix.
!   This rounded field replaces the addressed storage field.  If a signed
!   operation is specified, the contents of the accumulator sign byte
!   register replace the rightmost byte of the storage field after the
!   sign bit has been modified by the negative sign modifier.  The
!   contents of the accumulator and the sign byte register are not
!   changed by this operation.  The accumulator sign is ignored in the
!   actual rounding process."
!   Radix: "If a binary operation is specified, a binary one is added to
!   the field from the accumulator in the bit position immediately to the
!   right of the specified offset."
!   "Partial Field (PF); To-Memory Operation (MOP); Arithmetic Result
!   (RLZ, RZ, RGZ, RN).  These indicators are set as in STORE."
!   "Lost Carry (LC).  This indicator is turned on when the rounding
!   process causes a carry to be propagated beyond the left end of the
!   field stored."
!   Programming Notes: "An unsigned STORE ROUNDED addressing the
!   accumulator as the storage operand can also be used for this
!   purpose [rounding the accumulator]."  "A STORE ROUNDED with zero
!   offset specified is equivalent to a STORE."
! STORE, printed p.63: PF "if there is any one-bit in the accumulator to
! the left of the last bit position stored"; MOP "is turned on"; the
! result indicators "are set according to the data field stored.  The
! sign of the accumulator, as modified by the negative sign modifier,
! affects the setting whether it is stored or not."
!
! TWO READINGS ARE CHOSEN, and case 2 is the one that tells them apart:
!   PF is read from the accumulator AS IT STANDS (SRD does not change it),
!     not from the rounded quantity; the carry is LC's business.
!   LC is the carry out of the NUMERIC width (field length less the sign
!     byte when signed), docs/spec_factor.md 4.6; case 6 is signed.
!
! THE INDICATOR WORDS.  Each case loads its accumulator, then clears the
! register (Z,$IND), then does the SRD, then copies $IND out with L and
! ST -- the order decks/load_converted.strap uses, so the word is the
! SRD's alone.  IBM bit n is 2**(63-n): LC 22 = (16)20000000000, PF 23 =
! (16)10000000000, OP 15 = (16)1000000000000, MOP 55 = (16)100, RLZ 56 =
! (16)80, RZ 57 = (16)40, RGZ 58 = (16)20, RN 59 = (16)10.  Every target
! word starts as all ones, so the bits outside the field are checked too.
!
!   1 round up       acc (16)00AB80.  SRD(BU,8,8) at offset 8: AB, and
!                    the bit right of the offset is the 1 of 80: AC.
!                    T1 = (16)ACFFFFFFFFFFFFFF.  I1 = MOP, RGZ = (16)120.
!   2 carry out      acc (16)00FF80: FF + 1 = 100, the field stores 00
!                    and the carry leaves it: LC.  The accumulator above
!                    the field is zero, so PF stays off (PF FROM THE
!                    ROUNDED SUM WOULD TURN IT ON).  Stored field zero:
!                    RZ.  T2 = (16)00FFFFFFFFFFFFFF, I2 = (16)20000000140.
!   3 PF, no round   acc (16)01AB00: AB, the bit right of the offset 0,
!                    so AB; the 01 above it is PF.  T3 =
!                    (16)ABFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, I3 = (16)10000000120.
!   4 negative acc,  LN(BU,64,8) of 00AB80: the same magnitude, minus.
!     signed field   "The accumulator sign is ignored in the actual
!                    rounding process": AB rounds to AC.  SRD(B,16,8):
!                    eight numeric bits AC, then the sign byte register,
!                    zones 0000, sign 1, flags 000 = (16)08.  T4 =
!                    (16)AC08FFFFFFFFFFFF.  Result minus, not zero: RLZ,
!                    RN; I4 = (16)190.
!   5 offset 0       "equivalent to a STORE": nothing is added (there is
!                    no bit to the right of offset 0).  SRD(BU,16,8) at
!                    offset 0 of (16)00AB80 stores AB80.  T5 =
!                    (16)AB80FFFFFFFFFFFF, I5 = (16)120.
!   6 signed carry   acc (16)000FF8.  SRD(B,12,4) at offset 4: eight
!     across the     numeric bits FF, the bit right of the offset is the
!     numeric width  8's 1, FF + 1 = 100: numeric 00 and LC.  The sign
!                    nibble is the register's positions 4-7, sign plus
!                    and flags off, 0000.  T6 = (16)000FFFFFFFFFFFFF,
!                    I6 = LC, MOP, RZ = (16)20000000140.
!   7 carry through  acc (16)00A7F8.  SRD(BU,12,8) at offset 4: A7F, and
!     the field      the 1 of 8 carries through the four ones: A80.
!                    T7 = (16)A80FFFFFFFFFFFFF, I7 = (16)120.
!   8 into $R        The Programming Note's use.  acc right half
!                    (16)12C0.  SRD(BU,56,8), $R, 8: the field is
!                    accumulator bits 64-119, which IS word 9 bits 0-55,
!                    so the rounded value (16)12 + 1 = 13 goes back where
!                    it came from and bits 56-63 keep their C0: word 9 =
!                    (16)13C0, read out by ST into T8.
!  10 SRDN, signed   (16)00AB80, plus, SRDN(B,16,8) at offset 8: AC, and
!                    "the sign bit has been modified by the negative sign
!                    modifier": sign byte (16)08.  T10 = (16)AC08FFFFFFFFFFFF.
!                    The modified sign is minus: I10 = RLZ, RN, MOP = (16)190.
!  11 SRDN, unsigned SRDN(BU,8,8): "If the unsigned modifier is specified,
!                    the negative sign modifier has no effect on the field
!                    stored.  However, the result indicators are set
!                    according to the modified accumulator sign" (p.63): T11
!                    = (16)ACFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, I11 = (16)190.  This is what the
!                    printed "SRDN,$L" of C22-6578 4.9 does, at offset 0.
!   9 decimal        (run last) SRD(DU,8,4): refused, Operation Code Invalid, as the
!                    model refuses decimal arithmetic (the five added is a
!                    decimal addition; only the decimal UNSIGNED STORE is
!                    built).  T9 stays all ones; I9 = OP = (16)1000000000000.
!
! RUN (registered in tests/run_tests.sh):
!   cd stretch/tests && ./run_program.sh ../decks/vfl_srd.strap StretchVflSrdTb \
!       "PC=<HALT>" "T1:1110=0xACFFFFFFFFFFFFFF" ... (the line there)
!
! OBSERVED 2026-11-16: ALL TESTS PASSED, 17 checks and the PC, on the first
! run against the expectations above (worked before the run).  Cases 10
! and 11 were added after, and first run with case 9 ninth: their
! indicator words came out (16)1000000000190 -- the OP from case 9 still on
! after Z,$IND -- so case 9 was moved last; then all 21 checks pass.
!
! CYCLES=974 is the model's count, pinned (the line in run_tests.sh).
! INJECTED: StretchTiming.bsv's SRD term (Perf. Char. Vol. 1 Table 3's
! extra 1.2 us pre-execution, 4 clocks at a nonzero offset) set to 0:
! FAIL cycles = 934, 40 fewer = ten SRDs at a nonzero offset times 4 --
! cases 1-4, 6-8, 10, 11 and the refused decimal case 9, which is charged
! too; case 5 (offset 0) is not.
!
! MEASURED INJECTIONS in bsv/StretchExecute.bsv's ST arm, each on a copy,
! the arm restored from a saved copy and checked with cmp:
!   PF from the ROUNDED sum (the other reading)   FAIL I2, I6 (PF on:
!                                                 (16)30000000140) -- I6
!                                                 too, which was not
!                                                 predicted: its carry is
!                                                 above the numeric width
!   the negative modifier ignored by SRD          FAIL T10 (AC00), I10 and
!     (measured with all eleven cases)            I11 ((16)120, plus)
!   (the five below were measured with cases 1-9 only)
!   the one added AT the offset, not right of it  FAIL T3 alone (AC); T5
!                                                 does not move, because
!                                                 offset 0 adds nothing
!                                                 either way
!   LC never set                                  FAIL I2, I6 ((16)140)
!   the round subtracted for a minus accumulator  FAIL T4 alone (AB08)
!   SRD unbuilt (the model before 2026-11-16)     FAIL 15: T1-T7, I1-I7
!                                                 (OP), T8 (12C0); T9, I9
!                                                 and the PC pass, since
!                                                 decimal SRD is OP either
!                                                 way
!
! TIMING RE-PINNED 2026-11-16, 974 -> 1223 clocks, every value check unchanged.
! VFL E-box time now depends on the operation: bsv/StretchTiming.bsv's
! eboxClocks charges each operation the throughput Perf. Char. Vol. 2's
! atlas prints for it (docs/atlas_oracle.md).  SRD is charged ST's page (PDF
! 124/125, 18 + 2 bytes, 22.1 clocks under three bytes) plus the 4-clock
! Table 3 term at a nonzero offset, which stays; the loads, L's page (PDF
! 120).  The injection below, re-run 2026-11-16 at the new timing
! (srdRound forced to 0): FAIL cycles = 1183, 40 fewer than 1223 -- ten
! SRDs at a nonzero offset times 4, as before -- and nothing else.

        SLC, 1000.0
! -- 1. round up ---------------------------------------------------
START   L(BU,64,8), V1
        Z, $IND
        SRD(BU,8,8), T1, 8
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I1, 0
! -- 2. the carry leaves the field: LC, and PF off ------------------
        L(BU,64,8), V2
        Z, $IND
        SRD(BU,8,8), T2, 8
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I2, 0
! -- 3. a one above the field: PF -----------------------------------
        L(BU,64,8), V3
        Z, $IND
        SRD(BU,8,8), T3, 8
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I3, 0
! -- 4. a negative accumulator, a signed field ----------------------
        LN(BU,64,8), V1
        Z, $IND
        SRD(B,16,8), T4, 8
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I4, 0
! -- 5. offset 0 ----------------------------------------------------
        L(BU,64,8), V1
        Z, $IND
        SRD(BU,16,8), T5, 0
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I5, 0
! -- 6. a signed field, the carry crosses the numeric width ---------
        L(BU,64,8), V6
        Z, $IND
        SRD(B,12,4), T6, 4
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I6, 0
! -- 7. a carry through the field -----------------------------------
        L(BU,64,8), V7
        Z, $IND
        SRD(BU,12,8), T7, 4
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I7, 0
! -- 8. rounding the accumulator in place ---------------------------
        L(BU,64,8), V8
        SRD(BU,56,8), $R, 8
        ST(BU,64,8), T8, 0
! -- 10. the negative modifier, signed: the sign bit stored is 1 -----
        L(BU,64,8), V1
        Z, $IND
        SRDN(B,16,8), T10, 8
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I10, 0
! -- 11. the negative modifier, unsigned: field unchanged, minus ----
        L(BU,64,8), V1
        Z, $IND
        SRDN(BU,8,8), T11, 8
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I11, 0
! -- 9. decimal: refused.  Run LAST: OP (bit 15) set here was still on
!    in case 10's word after Z,$IND when this case ran ninth (observed).
        Z, $IND
        SRD(DU,8,4), T9, 4
        L(BU,64,8), $IND, 0
        ST(BU,64,8), I9, 0
HALT    BEW, $

        SLC, 1100.0
V1      DD(BU,64,8), (16)00AB80
V2      DD(BU,64,8), (16)00FF80
V3      DD(BU,64,8), (16)01AB00
V6      DD(BU,64,8), (16)000FF8
V7      DD(BU,64,8), (16)00A7F8
V8      DD(BU,64,8), (16)12C0

        SLC, 1110.0
T1      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T2      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T3      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T4      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T5      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T6      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T7      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T8      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T9      DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF

        SLC, 1120.0
I1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
I2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
I3      DD(BU,64,8), 0
I4      DD(BU,64,8), 0
I5      DD(BU,64,8), 0
I6      DD(BU,64,8), 0
I7      DD(BU,64,8), 0
I9      DD(BU,64,8), 0

        SLC, 1130.0
T10     DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
T11     DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
I10     DD(BU,64,8), 0
I11     DD(BU,64,8), 0

        END, START
